{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"code","value":"function injectQueuer<TValue, TSelected>(\n   fn,\n   options?,\nselector?): AngularQueuer<TValue, TSelected>;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/pacer/blob/main/packages/angular-pacer/src/queuer/injectQueuer.ts#L96","children":[{"type":"text","value":"queuer/injectQueuer.ts:96"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"An Angular function that creates and manages a Queuer instance."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This is a lower-level function that provides direct access to the Queuer's functionality.\nThis allows you to integrate it with any state management solution you prefer."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The Queuer processes items synchronously in order, with optional delays between processing each item.\nThe queuer includes an internal tick mechanism that can be started and stopped, making it useful as a scheduler."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"state-management-and-selector","children":[{"type":"text","value":"State Management and Selector"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The function uses TanStack Store for state management and wraps it with Angular signals.\nThe "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"selector"},{"type":"text","value":" parameter allows you to specify which state changes will trigger signal updates,\noptimizing performance by preventing unnecessary updates when irrelevant state changes occur."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"By default, there will be no reactive state subscriptions"}]},{"type":"text","value":" and you must opt-in to state\ntracking by providing a selector function. This prevents unnecessary updates and gives you\nfull control over when your component tracks state changes."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"type-parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"tvalue","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TValue"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TValue"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"tselected","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TSelected"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TSelected"},{"type":"text","value":" = {\n}"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"fn","children":[{"type":"text","value":"fn"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"item"},{"type":"text","value":") => "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"void"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"options?"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../type-aliases/AngularPacerOptions.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"AngularPacerOptions"}]},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"link","href":"../interfaces/AngularQueuerOptions.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"AngularQueuerOptions"}]},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TValue"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TSelected"},{"type":"text","value":">> = "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{}"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"selector","children":[{"type":"text","value":"selector?"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"state"},{"type":"text","value":") => "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TSelected"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"returns","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"../interfaces/AngularQueuer.md","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"AngularQueuer"}]},{"type":"text","value":"<"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TValue"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TSelected"},{"type":"text","value":">"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"example","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example"}]},{"type":"code","value":"// Default behavior - no reactive state subscriptions\nconst queue = injectQueuer(\n  (item) => console.log('Processing:', item),\n  { started: true, wait: 1000 }\n);\n\n// Opt-in to track queue contents changes\nconst queue = injectQueuer(\n  (item) => console.log('Processing:', item),\n  { started: true, wait: 1000 },\n  (state) => ({ items: state.items, size: state.size })\n);\n\n// Add items\nqueue.addItem('task1');\n\n// Access the selected state\nconst { items, isRunning } = queue.state();","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"cleanup-on-destroy","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Cleanup on Destroy"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"By default, the function stops the queuer when the component is destroyed.\nUse the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"onUnmount"},{"type":"text","value":" option to customize this. For example, to flush pending items instead:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const queue = injectQueuer(fn, {\n  started: true,\n  onUnmount: (q) => q.flush()\n});","lang":"ts"}],"headings":[{"id":"state-management-and-selector","text":"State Management and Selector","level":2},{"id":"type-parameters","text":"Type Parameters","level":2},{"id":"tvalue","text":"TValue","level":3},{"id":"tselected","text":"TSelected","level":3},{"id":"parameters","text":"Parameters","level":2},{"id":"fn","text":"fn","level":3},{"id":"options","text":"options?","level":3},{"id":"selector","text":"selector?","level":3},{"id":"returns","text":"Returns","level":2},{"id":"example","text":"Example","level":2},{"id":"cleanup-on-destroy","text":"Cleanup on Destroy","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n```ts\nfunction injectQueuer<TValue, TSelected>(\n   fn,\n   options?,\nselector?): AngularQueuer<TValue, TSelected>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [queuer/injectQueuer.ts:96](https://github.com/TanStack/pacer/blob/main/packages/angular-pacer/src/queuer/injectQueuer.ts#L96)\n\nAn Angular function that creates and manages a Queuer instance.\n\nThis is a lower-level function that provides direct access to the Queuer's functionality.\nThis allows you to integrate it with any state management solution you prefer.\n\nThe Queuer processes items synchronously in order, with optional delays between processing each item.\nThe queuer includes an internal tick mechanism that can be started and stopped, making it useful as a scheduler.\n\n## State Management and Selector\n\nThe function uses TanStack Store for state management and wraps it with Angular signals.\nThe `selector` parameter allows you to specify which state changes will trigger signal updates,\noptimizing performance by preventing unnecessary updates when irrelevant state changes occur.\n\n**By default, there will be no reactive state subscriptions** and you must opt-in to state\ntracking by providing a selector function. This prevents unnecessary updates and gives you\nfull control over when your component tracks state changes.\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### TValue\n\n`TValue`\n\n### TSelected\n\n`TSelected` = \\{\n\\}\n\n## Parameters\n\n### fn\n\n(`item`) => `void`\n\n### options?\n\n[`AngularPacerOptions`](../type-aliases/AngularPacerOptions.md)\\<[`AngularQueuerOptions`](../interfaces/AngularQueuerOptions.md)\\<`TValue`, `TSelected`\\>\\> = `{}`\n\n### selector?\n\n(`state`) => `TSelected`\n\n## Returns\n\n[`AngularQueuer`](../interfaces/AngularQueuer.md)\\<`TValue`, `TSelected`\\>\n\n## Example\n\n```ts\n// Default behavior - no reactive state subscriptions\nconst queue = injectQueuer(\n  (item) => console.log('Processing:', item),\n  { started: true, wait: 1000 }\n);\n\n// Opt-in to track queue contents changes\nconst queue = injectQueuer(\n  (item) => console.log('Processing:', item),\n  { started: true, wait: 1000 },\n  (state) => ({ items: state.items, size: state.size })\n);\n\n// Add items\nqueue.addItem('task1');\n\n// Access the selected state\nconst { items, isRunning } = queue.state();\n```\n\n## Cleanup on Destroy\n\nBy default, the function stops the queuer when the component is destroyed.\nUse the `onUnmount` option to customize this. For example, to flush pending items instead:\n\n```ts\nconst queue = injectQueuer(fn, {\n  started: true,\n  onUnmount: (q) => q.flush()\n});\n```\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: injectQueuer\ntitle: injectQueuer\n---\n\n```ts\nfunction injectQueuer<TValue, TSelected>(\n   fn,\n   options?,\nselector?): AngularQueuer<TValue, TSelected>;\n```\n\nDefined in: [queuer/injectQueuer.ts:96](https://github.com/TanStack/pacer/blob/main/packages/angular-pacer/src/queuer/injectQueuer.ts#L96)\n\nAn Angular function that creates and manages a Queuer instance.\n\nThis is a lower-level function that provides direct access to the Queuer's functionality.\nThis allows you to integrate it with any state management solution you prefer.\n\nThe Queuer processes items synchronously in order, with optional delays between processing each item.\nThe queuer includes an internal tick mechanism that can be started and stopped, making it useful as a scheduler.\n\n## State Management and Selector\n\nThe function uses TanStack Store for state management and wraps it with Angular signals.\nThe `selector` parameter allows you to specify which state changes will trigger signal updates,\noptimizing performance by preventing unnecessary updates when irrelevant state changes occur.\n\n**By default, there will be no reactive state subscriptions** and you must opt-in to state\ntracking by providing a selector function. This prevents unnecessary updates and gives you\nfull control over when your component tracks state changes.\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### TValue\n\n`TValue`\n\n### TSelected\n\n`TSelected` = \\{\n\\}\n\n## Parameters\n\n### fn\n\n(`item`) => `void`\n\n### options?\n\n[`AngularPacerOptions`](../type-aliases/AngularPacerOptions.md)\\<[`AngularQueuerOptions`](../interfaces/AngularQueuerOptions.md)\\<`TValue`, `TSelected`\\>\\> = `{}`\n\n### selector?\n\n(`state`) => `TSelected`\n\n## Returns\n\n[`AngularQueuer`](../interfaces/AngularQueuer.md)\\<`TValue`, `TSelected`\\>\n\n## Example\n\n```ts\n// Default behavior - no reactive state subscriptions\nconst queue = injectQueuer(\n  (item) => console.log('Processing:', item),\n  { started: true, wait: 1000 }\n);\n\n// Opt-in to track queue contents changes\nconst queue = injectQueuer(\n  (item) => console.log('Processing:', item),\n  { started: true, wait: 1000 },\n  (state) => ({ items: state.items, size: state.size })\n);\n\n// Add items\nqueue.addItem('task1');\n\n// Access the selected state\nconst { items, isRunning } = queue.state();\n```\n\n## Cleanup on Destroy\n\nBy default, the function stops the queuer when the component is destroyed.\nUse the `onUnmount` option to customize this. For example, to flush pending items instead:\n\n```ts\nconst queue = injectQueuer(fn, {\n  started: true,\n  onUnmount: (q) => q.flush()\n});\n```\n"}
